Package: WdStar
Type: Package
Title: Distance-Based Multivariate Welch ANOVA
Version: 2.5.4
Description: The WdStar package is designed to improve the statistical robustness of multivariate data analyses by implementing distance-based multivariate Welch analysis of variance for comparing groups with unequal dispersion, as described by Hamidi et al. (2019) <doi:10.1186/s40168-019-0659-9>. Also provides the two-group distance-based Welch t-test of Alekseyenko (2016) <doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btw524>. The methods address potential confounding of location and dispersion effects in multivariate analyses, and support stratified permutation tests and covariate adjustment of a principal-coordinate representation to remove confounding or technical variables. The methods have general applicability in microbiome and other ‘omics data analyses.
License: GPL (>=3) 
URL: https://github.com/alekseyenko/WdStar
BugReports: https://github.com/alekseyenko/WdStar/issues
